From 50798f69b25abd7d8a89dc70f696810d4b3450d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sixvolts <rigel@sixvolts.org>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 13:00:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda: fuse the GDN gate ADD -> SOFTPLUS -> MUL and the beta
 SIGMOID

qwen35 recurrent layers compute softplus(alpha + dt_bias) * ssm_a and
sigmoid(beta) on 32-48 element vectors: an add, a fused softplus-mul and
a sigmoid launch per layer per token. One kernel now does all three, in
the ops' arithmetic; the SIGMOID is folded in when it is the next
non-view node and independent of the gate. Matched with ggml_can_fuse:
ggml_cuda_can_fuse rejects patterns outside its whitelist.
GGML_CUDA_NO_ADD_UNARY_FUSION=1 disables it.

Qwen3.5-4B decode with the residual add-norm fusion: launches per step
745 -> 634, kernel time 8.61 -> 8.27 ms, tg256 111.9 -> 119.3 tok/s
(3 interleaved runs each); PPL identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DTjwwGh3znQpq4Yoxunx6b
